  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. Enhanced decent work statistics using innovative sources and statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">A.The Public Ministry of Labour of Minas Gerais and the Secretariat of Labour Inspection - SIT (of the Ministry of Labour and Employment), with support of ILO, defined the construction of an Informational Tool, in digital format whose purpose is to provide relevant information to institutions involved in the fight against forced labour and child labour in the coffee production chain in the state of Minas Gerais. The indicators that make up the tool are the result of partnerships between the ILO and the various information-producing bodies of the National Statistical System. B. In 2022 and 2023, the indicators of the five Smartlab Platform observatories were updated. The ILO, in close relationship with the Public Labour Ministry, which manages the platform, managed to articulate with important information-generating bodies, such as the Ministry of Justice, Ministry of Citizenship, Federal Highway Police and others, to create new content for the platform. Through the SmartLab Decent Work Series , three events were held to launch updates in 2022 on the themes of Child Labour, Slave Labour and OSH and four events in 2023 (Child Labour, Forced Labour, OSH and Diversity and Equal Opportunities). C. The ILO, in partnership with the Undersecretariat for Statistics and Labour Studies of the Ministry of Labour and Employment and with the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics (IBGE), made possible the documented systematization of the construction process of labour administrative records in the country. The purpose of the publication is the historical record of administrative records, in addition to analysing the changes that may occur in these systems and their integration for the improvement of public policies in general. It also serves as a reference for sharing and disseminating the Brazilian experience with other countries, notably in the context of South-South Cooperation. The ILO technically contributed to the elaboration of the Informational Tool defining the content, regionalization, thematic areas, pedagogical functionalities and operationalized the process of contracting a specialized consultancy for the construction of digital tools (where dashboards of indicators and other relevant information for actors and institutions are available). In addition, it directly contributed to the construction of several datasets of indicators that fed into the platform. Also directly contributed to the production and selection of new thematic content, development of database and analytical texts to update the Smartlab Platform observatories; in the mobilization for the collaboration of new partners for the project, which made possible the expansion of the observatories with new themes and indicators.</narrative>
   </description>
